# Cloudflare Pages routing for majstr.pro (https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/).
#
# The app's routes are LISTED, not caught by a `/* /index.html 200`. The catch-all answered every
# path with 200 and the landing's HTML — /api/, //feed/, any typo — so search engines found the
# landing at a dozen addresses (SEO audit 2026-10). Unknown paths now fall to /404.html with a real
# 404; a file that exists (assets, /og/, the calculator pages, robots.txt) is served before these.
#
# ⚠️ A NEW top-level route in src/routes/routes.tsx must be added here, or a refresh, a shared link,
# an email/push link or the monobank return lands on 404. `src/routes/redirects.test.ts` reads
# both files and fails when one is missing. An installed PWA is not affected either way: its service
# worker answers navigations from the cached app shell.
#
# 200 = rewrite: the URL stays, the router reads it on boot. The destination is "/", NOT
# "/index.html": Pages' pretty URLs answer /index.html with a 308 to "/", so a rewrite to it turned
# /login into a redirect to the landing and every /projects/:id into a 404 (seen in
# `wrangler pages dev`). Rewriting to "/" serves the same index.html with the URL intact.

# Partner alias. A 301 to the landing carrying the partner as ?ref= — main.tsx records it first-touch
# on boot, exactly as the client-side /liga route did — so the alias is no longer a second copy of
# the landing in the index.
/liga                  /?ref=liga     301
/liga/                 /?ref=liga     301

/login                 /               200
/register              /               200
/verify-email          /               200
/forgot-password       /               200
/reset-password        /               200
/privacy               /               200
/new                   /               200
/finance               /               200
/profile               /               200
/templates             /               200
/projects              /               200
/projects/*            /               200
/catalog               /               200
/catalog/*             /               200
/estimates/*           /               200
/acts/*                /               200
/shopping/*            /               200
/receipts/*            /               200
/billing/*             /               200
# The service worker's fallback when a push carries no url.
/dashboard             /               200
